Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.35,0:00:09.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Hello friends! Today we'll understand the complete Claude AI interface, right from the start, step by step.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.40,0:00:20.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Every option on the screen: what it is, how to use it, when to use it, and its limits, all in detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.03,0:00:32.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}At the end, we'll watch a real Claude Code terminal demo where Claude understands a project and fixes a real bug. So watch till the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.43,0:00:41.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}This is Claude's home screen. I'm on the Pro plan, which is why 'Pro' appears next to my name at the bottom.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.91,0:00:47.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}This screen is easy to understand, because it has three main parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.41,0:00:54.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}First, the sidebar on the left, with all the main options and your past chats.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.71,0:01:01.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Second, the message box in the middle, where you ask questions or give Claude tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.78,0:01:08.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And third, your account in the bottom-left corner, which opens Settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.10,0:01:21.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Note: some options may look a little different depending on your plan, account and app version, so don't worry if your screen differs slightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.08,0:01:32.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now let's go through the sidebar one by one. At the top is New. Click it and a brand-new, empty chat starts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.56,0:01:45.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Each chat is its own conversation, so start a new chat whenever the topic changes. One topic per chat keeps answers focused.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.16,0:01:53.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Below it is Search. It helps you quickly find your old chats.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.44,0:02:12.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Paid plans like Pro also have chat search: ask Claude what you discussed about a topic, and it searches your past chats. Turn it on or off in Settings › Your Claude.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.99,0:02:23.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Next is Projects. A project is a separate workspace where you keep your files and instructions in one place.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.26,0:02:36.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Every chat you create inside that project uses these files as background knowledge, like your notes, documents or code.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.22,0:02:52.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Creating one is simple: open Projects, click New Project, add a name and description, add files with the plus button, and use Set project instructions to tell Claude how to respond.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.58,0:03:12.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Remember: project chats don't share their conversations, only the project knowledge. Paid plans can grow project knowledge up to 10× with RAG. Sharing projects is for Team and Enterprise only.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.16,0:03:25.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Next is Artifacts: things Claude makes for you, like documents, code, small websites, diagrams or dashboards.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.14,0:03:40.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}They open in a separate panel next to the chat, and all of them are saved on the Artifacts page, so you can reopen them any time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.86,0:04:00.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Ask for edits in the chat, and export documents to Word, PDF, Markdown or Google Docs. They start private. They need 'Code execution and file creation' turned on in Settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.01,0:04:16.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now Code. It opens Claude Code, an agentic coding tool: it doesn't just write code, it reads your project files, edits them and can run commands.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.53,0:04:27.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}On the web, first connect your GitHub account, pick a repository, and describe your task in plain language.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.44,0:04:40.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Claude works in the cloud on a separate machine. When it's done, you review every change in the diff and, if it looks right, click Create PR.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.81,0:04:53.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Claude Code is also in the Terminal, VS Code, JetBrains and the Desktop app. It's included in Pro, but it counts toward your usage limits.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.73,0:05:05.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Below is Customize, where you extend what Claude can do. It has three things: Skills, Connectors and Plugins.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.09,0:05:17.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Skills teach Claude how to do specific tasks. Connectors link Claude to outside services: click Connect and sign in,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.66,0:05:27.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}and Plugins bundle skills and commands. Use the Discover tab to find new ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.08,0:05:39.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now Usage: see how much of your plan you've used. Full details are on the Usage page in Settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.28,0:05:56.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}On Pro, the session limit resets every 5 hours, plus a weekly limit. If you run out, usage credits let you keep working. Tip: lower effort uses less.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.03,0:06:07.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Chats and tasks lists your recent chats and tasks. Click View all to see the full list.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.16,0:06:20.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Hover over any chat for the three-dot menu to rename or delete it. You can also select several chats and delete them together.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.53,0:06:31.01,Cap,,840,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now click your name in the bottom-left corner. That opens Settings, and it also shows your plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.02,0:06:43.90,Cap,,840,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In Settings: Appearance changes the theme, Your Claude holds memory and chat search, and Usage shows your limits and credits.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.64,0:06:57.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Look at the top-right corner: this small ghost icon starts an incognito chat, from a new chat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.33,0:07:13.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Incognito chats aren't saved to history or memory and aren't used for training. But they can't be reopened once closed, and aren't available in projects.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.17,0:07:24.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now the message box in the middle: the most important part, because this is where you type your question or task.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.23,0:07:38.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A simple formula for good answers: say what you want, for whom, and in what format. For example: explain Python lists to a beginner with 3 examples.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.83,0:07:52.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}On the left of the message box is the plus button: choose Add files or photos to attach files. Drag and drop or paste also work.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.58,0:08:05.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}PDF, Word, Excel, CSV, text and images are supported: up to 20 files per chat, each up to 500 MB.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.36,0:08:15.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The same plus menu can turn memory off for a single chat, as long as you do it before the first message.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.62,0:08:24.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Next to plus is the Chat / Cowork switch. Chat is for normal conversation and quick questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.85,0:08:32.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In Cowork you hand Claude a whole task and it works through the steps itself,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.42,0:08:42.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}like researching the web, reading your files, and producing finished spreadsheets or presentations.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.25,0:08:57.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Cowork uses more usage, is for paid plans, and needs the Claude Desktop app for local files. Always check its permission setting before it acts.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.14,0:09:07.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now the model selector on the right: Opus 5.5 with Medium effort is selected.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.63,0:09:21.07,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Click the model name to pick another model; More models has extra options. You can switch mid-chat; it applies from the next reply.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.08,0:09:33.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The same menu has Effort: how deeply Claude thinks before answering. Five levels: Low, Medium, High, Extra high and Max.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.80,0:09:44.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Higher effort gives more detailed, careful answers, but takes longer and uses more.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.83,0:10:00.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Medium is fine for everyday work; choose High or above for hard coding, planning or long documents. Opus 5.5 always thinks before answering.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.14,0:10:10.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Next to the model are the mic and voice buttons, so you can speak to Claude instead of typing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.51,0:10:23.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Below the message box are Write, Learn, Code, Life stuff and Claude's choice: if you're not sure what to ask, they give you ideas to start.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.59,0:10:33.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now the most interesting part: a real Claude Code demo, right in the terminal. Everything you see here really ran.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.76,0:10:53.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}To install Claude Code, run the official command: curl on Mac, Linux and WSL, irm on Windows PowerShell. Then check with claude --version. The first run asks you to log in.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.93,0:11:04.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}This is a small demo project, a to-do app, with files like app.py, storage.py and tasks.json.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.05,0:11:12.81,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now I give Claude Code a simple instruction: explain this project's files in 3 short points.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.82,0:11:20.83,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Claude Code is now reading all the project files. We've fast-forwarded this wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.84,0:11:35.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Look: Claude clearly explained each file. Best of all, it spotted a bug on its own: list_tasks reads the 'name' key, but the data uses 'title'.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.06,0:11:43.87,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Let's see that bug for real. Running the app throws a KeyError: the 'name' key doesn't exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.88,0:11:50.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}So I tell Claude Code about this error and ask it to find and fix the bug.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.34,0:11:58.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Notice: in this command I used --allowedTools to permit file edits only, nothing else.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.93,0:12:05.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Claude Code is reading the code and preparing a fix. This part is fast-forwarded too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.06,0:12:18.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Claude fixed the bug, and said running the app to test it needed approval, which I hadn't given, so it found the cause by reading the code.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.38,0:12:33.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}That's Claude Code's key safety feature: reading files needs no permission, but it asks before changing files or running commands, unless you allowed it in advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.25,0:12:44.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Now we review the exact change with git diff: red is the old line, green the new. Just 'name' replaced by 'title', a one-line change.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.53,0:12:51.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Run the app again and both tasks print correctly. Bug fixed!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.91,0:13:13.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Claude Code has four permission modes. Manual, the default, asks the first time each tool is used. Accept edits accepts file edits automatically. Plan only reads and plans. Auto lets a safety classifier review actions for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.80,0:13:22.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}If you're a beginner, start with Manual or Plan mode, so every change passes your review.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.07,0:13:27.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Before we finish, some very important points.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.67,0:13:37.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}First, AI can make mistakes, so always verify Claude's answers and code yourself, especially for important work.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.00,0:13:45.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Second, never share passwords, API keys or any private data in a chat.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.75,0:13:52.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Third, review every change Claude Code makes in the diff before you run it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.29,0:14:01.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Fourth, remember that even Pro has usage limits, so plan big tasks carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.32,0:14:12.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In the next videos of this series, we'll learn Projects, Artifacts, Cowork, settings and Claude Code one by one, in even more detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.90,0:14:27.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}If you learned something new, like the video, share it with friends, and subscribe with the bell icon. See you in the next video. Thank you!
